+// LIGHTHOUSE_IOS (overlay 0031 rev2): DEEPER ON iOS. Fast3D transforms
+// vertices on the CPU and sub-allocates every draw from this shared pool;
+// the slot index advances once per EndFrame. Nothing fences reuse -- in 2D
+// nothing has to, because the drawable acquire bounds CPU run-ahead below
+// the pool depth by construction. The stereo path acquires no drawable AND
+// advances the pool once per EYE (twice per sub-frame), so at depth 3 a slot
+// is recycled every 1.5 sub-frames (~12 ms at 120 fps). Once GPU lag exceeds
+// that under load, the CPU overwrites vertices the GPU has not drawn yet and
+// one eye rasterizes the other eye's positions -- the reported left/right
+// flicker. Soh3DThrottle bounds the lag; this gives it headroom to work in:
+// 2 pairs in flight x (2 eyes + 1 building) = 6 live slots <= 8. ~25 MB.
